# Shadcn Components Usage Rules

## CRITICAL: Always Use Shadcn CLI

**❌ NEVER create custom UI components when Shadcn equivalents exist**

**✅ ALWAYS use Shadcn CLI:**

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add input card label checkbox --yes
```

## Naming Convention

**✅ Rename to PascalCase after installation:**

```bash
mv input.tsx Input.tsx && mv card.tsx Card.tsx
```

## Common Components Available

Check these before creating any UI component:

**Form**: input, label, checkbox, select, textarea, switch, radio-group
**Layout**: card, separator, aspect-ratio
**Navigation**: button, dropdown-menu, navigation-menu
**Feedback**: alert, toast, dialog, popover

## Import Pattern

**✅ Import from atoms:**
```typescript
import { Button } from '@/components/atoms/Button'
```

**❌ Don't create custom:**
```typescript
const Button = () => { /* custom */ } // Wrong
```

## Customization

**✅ Use CSS variables:**
```css
:root {
  --card: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
}
```

**❌ Don't wrap unnecessarily:**
```typescript
// Wrong
const CustomInput = (props) => <Input className="custom" {...props} />
// Right
<Input className="custom" {...props} />
```

## Summary

1. Check Shadcn first
2. Use CLI installation
3. Rename to PascalCase
4. Import from @/components/atoms
5. Customize via CSS variables
